  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Tax Work For Women-Zimbabwe Coalition on Debt and Development (Zimbabwe)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intersection between tax justice, gender equality and care continues to remain as an area of increasing concern, and an opportunity to influence. In Zimbabwe, efforts have been made to support the greater integration of the Ministries of Women Affairs and Health and Childcare into macroeconomic decision-making processes. The Making Tax Work for Women project will zero in on this integration with key government institutions and relevant revenue authorities, connecting with decision-making towards the lives of domestic care workers through partnership with domestic worker associations. Partners will focus on pushing for equitable tax reforms, through analysis and popularization of existing and new policies, policy briefs and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
